                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/6082: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-07T13:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                                1920—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 7—12:58
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Minister of Finance and several other officials of the Kolchak Cabinet passed
                    Harbin. Indications are that Kolchak Government also thing of the past. Semenoff
                    is issuing orders, appointing generals, creating commissions, and conferring
                    decorations. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
